cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CGE-Core, please cite CGE-Core as software and also cite the
  original PyCGE and the relevant underlying model source(s) for the model
  family you use.
title: "CGE-Core: a practitioner-first computable general equilibrium toolkit"
type: software

authors:
  - name: "CGE-Core contributors"

contact:
  - family-names: Miraflor
    given-names: James Matthew
    email: jbmiraflor@up.edu.ph
    affiliation: "Scientific Computing Laboratory, Department of Computer Science, University of the Philippines Diliman"

version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-08-30"
repository-code: "https://github.com/miraflor/CGE-core"
license: MIT

keywords:
  - cge
  - computable-general-equilibrium
  - pyomo
  - economics
  - policy-simulation
  - social-accounting-matrix
  - ifpri-standard-cge
  - camcge

abstract: >-
  CGE-Core is an open-source, maintained and extended fork of PyCGE that
  provides a common Python workflow for several computable general equilibrium
  model traditions. The repository includes practitioner-facing APIs, tests,
  documentation, validation workflows, packaging, tutorials, and additional
  implementation work. Inherited PyCGE code and the underlying published
  economic model specifications retain their original provenance. Development
  of the fork has been substantially AI-assisted, with human maintenance and
  review. The project therefore uses collective project authorship for software
  citation; James Matthew Miraflor is listed as maintainer/contact rather than
  as the sole software author.

